// endpoint_roll_out_landing.proto — RollOutLanding: agent-repl's deploy hook
// asks the daemon to roll out what a deploy landed. RUNTIME section.
//
// THE DAEMON OWNS ITS ROLLOUTS. agent-repl's repository describes its deploy
// stage as a script (`modules/app/agent-repl/bin/deploy-landing.sh`) that
// calls this rpc; the rollout itself -- build, install, restart what is out of
// date, the handover -- is the daemon's, exactly as agentrepl.v1.Deploy
// describes it.
//
// WITH A LEDGER, THE ROLLOUT IS REGISTERED, NOT STARTED. The deploy named by
// `deploy` is still running (its hook is what called), and its report to an
// async merge's requester is composed only as it ends. So the daemon records
// that the deploy's landing rolls out, and fires the rollout at the deploy's
// teardown, after the report is owed to it: the report then arrives only once
// the build carrying the landing is running. Landings that arrive while a
// rollout runs are covered by one rollout after it, never one per landing.
//
